<ArticleLayout slug="singles-day-618-production-calendar" ctaLabel="Plan the cycle with us" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Every page ranking for this explains what Singles Day is or how much it sold. None prints the platforms' own dated milestones, and none counts a production schedule back from them. This page does both, and it is careful about which half is reported and which half is arithmetic.</p>

  <h2>When do Singles Day assets have to be ready?</h2>

  <p>Before the presale opens, and the presale date is the one milestone the platforms announce and the press reports with exact timestamps. For Tmall in 2025 that was 8:00 p.m. on 15 October. How long before that date production has to start is published by no platform, no government notice and no survey. So everything that follows separates the reported dates from the schedule counted back from them.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">No platform rule, government notice or survey found in September 2026 publishes how long creative production should take before a Singles Day or 618 deadline. The lead times in circulation come from companies selling preparation services, with no sample and no method behind them.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: search of Chinese- and English-language sources, 10 September 2026, covering reporting of platform rules and the pages ranking for four buyer phrasings. An observation about the published record, not a measurement.</p>

  <h2>What are the Tmall presale milestones?</h2>

  <p>All times below are Beijing time, and every date carries its platform and year, because the dates move and a date without a year is how a stale schedule ends up in a brief.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Tmall's 2025 Singles Day presale opened with a warm-up at 2:00 p.m. on 15 October, took deposits from 8:00 p.m. that evening until 5:59 p.m. on 20 October, and opened the spot sale at 8:00 p.m. on 20 October, running to 11:59 p.m. on 14 November.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese technology and ecommerce trade press reprinting Tmall's published 2025 Double 11 rules, 24 September 2025. Two outlets carried the platform's timetable the same day, with identical timestamps.</p>

  <p>The rules themselves arrive later than most planning assumes.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Tmall's 2025 Singles Day rules became public 21 days before its presale opened.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese trade press reporting the platform's rules on 24 September 2025, against a presale opening of 15 October 2025. Date arithmetic on two reported dates.</p>

  <p>Twenty-one days between the rules and the presale is not a production window. It is a confirmation window. Anything that needs to be shot, generated, retouched and approved has to be underway well before the rules that govern it are public.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Tmall opened its Singles Day presale at 8:00 p.m. on 24 October in 2023 and at 8:00 p.m. on 14 October in 2024, ten days earlier, then at 8:00 p.m. on 15 October in 2025, one day later.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese financial press reporting the platform's announcements, 21 October 2023, 13 October 2024 and 24 September 2025. Opening dates as announced by the platform for each year.</p>

  <p>That sequence matters more than any single date. The start moved ten days earlier into 2024 and then one day later in 2025. It does not simply move earlier every year, and a plan that assumes it does will start earlier than it needs to, or be wrong-footed the year it does not.</p>

  <h2>JD and Douyin run their own clocks</h2>

  <blockquote class="evidence">JD opened its Singles Day sale at 8:00 p.m. on 23 October in 2023, with no presale, at 8:00 p.m. on 14 October in 2024, and at 8:00 p.m. on 9 October in 2025, running to 14 November that year.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: JD's own corporate blog, 11 October 2024, and Chinese financial and trade press reporting the platform's announcements, 21 October 2023 and 28 September 2025. Opening dates as announced by the platform.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Douyin's ecommerce arm scheduled its 2025 Singles Day sale to open at midnight on 9 October and close at 11:59 p.m. on 11 November, inside a combined promotion period that began on 16 September.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese ecommerce trade press reporting the platform's published schedule, 28 September 2025. Dates as scheduled by the platform.</p>

