  <p>In 2025 JD and Douyin both opened on 9 October, six days before Tmall's presale. A brand selling on all three is not producing to one date. It is producing to the earliest one.</p>

  <p>No platform has announced 2026 Singles Day dates as of 10 September 2026. In 2025 the Tmall rules came out on 24 September, so the 2026 dates may land within weeks of this page's review date. Check before planning to them.</p>

  <h2>What does the 618 cycle look like?</h2>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Tmall opened its 618 presale on 26 May in 2023. In 2024 it dropped the official presale and opened the first sales wave at 8:00 p.m. on 20 May. In 2025 the presale opened at 8:00 p.m. on 13 May. In 2026 the event opened on 21 May, eight days later than the year before.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese state-wire, municipal and financial press reporting the platform's announcements, 24 May 2023, 7 May 2024, 8 May 2025 and 29 April 2026. Opening dates as published in each year's rules or launch notice.</p>

  <p>Eight days later in 2026. That is the second counterexample on this page to the idea that the calendar only ever moves forward.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Tmall published its 2025 618 rules and opened product registration on 8 May, five days before the presale opened at 8:00 p.m. on 13 May.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese financial press reporting the platform's rules, 8 and 9 May 2025. Two outlets; the day count is arithmetic on the reported dates.</p>

  <p>Five days. On the 2025 618 cycle, a brand waiting for the rules before starting production would have had less than a week.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Tmall's 2026 618 rules ran a presale from 21 May to 3 June alongside two spot-sale waves, 21 to 30 May and 31 May to 21 June, and, as reported, required presale products to be live before the presale warm-up began and spot products to be live by 10:00 p.m. on the first day of sale.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese ecommerce trade press reporting the platform's 2026 merchant rules, 29 April 2026, with the dates restated in a technology news roundup on 2 May 2026. Rules as reported, not read from the platform's rule center.</p>

  <p>That listing rule is the closest thing to a published asset deadline anywhere in this research, and it applies to Tmall's 2026 618 cycle as reported. It should not be assumed for JD or for Singles Day.</p>

  <p>One conflict in the 2026 record needs stating rather than resolving by average.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Consumer shopping guides in May 2026 printed a 12 or 13 May start for Tmall's 618. Reporting of the platform's own 2026 merchant rules gave 21 May.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese consumer guides and trade press, April and May 2026. The conflict is published rather than resolved by average; the reported rules are preferred because they carry the full wave structure.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">JD ran a warm-up season from 13 to 29 May 2026, opened its 618 sale at 8:00 p.m. on 30 May, and ran it to 21 June.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: Chinese technology press reporting the platform's launch announcement, 18 May 2026. Dates as stated by the platform's marketing center at launch.</p>

